               </text>
            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 81-year-old female patient. She was admitted on 12/10/2001 with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, presenting with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. On admission, physical examination, pulse oximetry, arterial blood gas analysis, chest X-ray, and blood tests were performed, confirming an acute exacerbation without evidence of pneumonia or cardiac decompensation. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. She responded well to treatment with notable clinical improvement. She is discharged in stable condition with an adjusted inhaler regimen and a short course of oral steroids. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
